class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>fx, fy, cx, cy px</th><th>Lever mm</th><th>log(R) rad</th><th>td ms</th><th>t_ga ms</th><th>Reprojection px</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>448.1, 447.5, 371.8, 280.9</td><td>[+32.6, −80.9, +27.9]</td><td>[+0.0031, −2.2167, +2.2213]</td><td>−4.32</td><td></td><td>0.294</td></tr><tr><th>cam1</th><td>286.8, 286.4, 415.7, 403.0</td><td>[+66.4, −111.0, −26.8]</td><td>[+0.0180, +2.2310, −2.2116]</td><td>−5.01</td><td></td><td>0.213</td></tr><tr><th>cam2</th><td>286.7, 286.2, 415.2, 397.4</td><td>[+2.5, −110.4, −26.7]</td><td>[−0.0255, −2.2259, +2.2122]</td><td>−7.68</td><td></td><td>0.226</td></tr><tr><th>IMU (base)</th><td></td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>−0.28 ± 0.04</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>IMU gx3_25</th><td></td><td>[−122.5, −47.0, −3.2]</td><td>[+2.2382, +2.2040, −0.0239]</td><td>+0.00</td><td>+0.19 ± 0.03</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>IMU gx3_35</th><td></td><td>[−81.9, −47.2, −3.6]</td><td>[−2.2182, −2.2243, +0.0157]</td><td>−1.55</td><td>+0.15 ± 0.03</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>IMU t265</th><td></td><td>[+56.0, −107.2, −31.0]</td><td>[+1.5788, +0.0068, −0.0022]</td><td>+2.88</td><td>−6.62 ± 0.03</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Lever arms and rotations are each sensor in the base IMU frame; rotation is log(R) in rad. td is the time offset to the base IMU, t_imu = t_sensor + td. Reprojection is the median per camera (all cameras: median 0.253 px): how well the model fits the corners, not how accurate it is.</p>", "check": "<div class=ex-callout><p><b>No published reference.</b> No published calibration exists for this rig, so this page has nothing to compare against. What we can show is how much each value moves from one recording to the next. <a href=\"/benchmark/results/virig-4imus-3cams/\">All 10 recordings and three tools: Dataset eval →</a></p></div>", "config": "<p>The marked lines are the choices that matter for this rig:</p><ul class=list><li><code>input.imu_topics</code>: Four IMU topics. The first is the base IMU; the other three are solved against it.</li><li><code>input.window_mode</code>: MVIS picks the 80 s window with the most motion.</li><li><code>camera_input.cameras</code>: The two T265 cameras are added to the graph at 4 Hz, which keeps the solve small.</li><li><code>solve.sigma_g</code>: IMU noise from a still recording of this rig, measured density × 2.5. The other three sigmas are set the same way.</li><li><code>estimate.board_points</code>: The printed board is not quite flat, so its shape is estimated too.</li><li><code>estimate.camera.intrinsics</code>: Camera intrinsics stay free in the camera + IMU solve.</li></ul><p class=note>This is the config of the run on this page, with every path cut to its file name. Point the paths at your copy.</p><p>The solve took about 13 min on one desktop. It writes <code>cam_imu.json</code>, a calibration YAML and a report beside the config.</p><dl class=ex-kv><dt>MVIS</dt><dd>MVIS main, measured-noise batch of 2026-11-08</dd><dt>Run date</dt><dd>2026-11-08</dd><dt>Data</dt><dd><a href=\"/reference/datasets/virig-4imus-3cams/\">VI-Rig 4 IMUs + 3 cams dataset page →</a></dd><dt>Config</dt><dd><code>virig_4imus_3cams_cam_imu.yaml</code>, above</dd><dt>Command</dt><dd><code>mvis cam-imu -c virig_4imus_3cams_cam_imu.yaml</code></dd></dl>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div><ul class=list><li>Recording april_01, one of the 10 recordings of this rig. MVIS picks the 80 s window with the most motion.</li><li>Cameras: a Blackfly S (pinhole with radial-tangential distortion) and the two T265 fisheye cameras (equidistant lens model).</li><li>IMUs: the Xsens MTi is the base IMU; the two MicroStrain units and the T265&#x27;s own IMU are solved against it.</li><li>Board: AprilGrid 6×6, tag 88 mm, spacing 0.3, t36h11.</li><li>Solve window: 80.0 s.</li></ul><p>Download: <a href=\"/reference/datasets/virig-4imus-3cams/\">VI-Rig 4 IMUs + 3 cams dataset page →</a> The recordings are listed there, not copied here.</p></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-52.8 -52.8 765.6 765.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"AprilGrid 6 by 6, to scale\"><rect x=\"-52.8\" y=\"-52.8\" width=\"765.6\" height=\"765.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path fill=\"#111\" d=\"M-26.40 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 545.60h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 545.60h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 545.60h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 545.60h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 545.60h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 545.60h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 545.60h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 660.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 660.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 660.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 660.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 660.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 660.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 660.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM0.00 0.00h88.00v88.00h-88.00zM1